{
  "layperson_summary": "This extension is a cookie manager that can view, edit, and delete cookies for any website you visit. It can also copy all of your cookies from every site at once to your computer's clipboard, where other programs on your computer could potentially read them. The most important thing to weigh is whether you need a tool with such broad access to all your browsing data, given this bulk export capability.",
  "technical_summary": "The extension requests broad access via the cookies and <all_urls> permissions, enabling read, write, and delete operations over all domains (finding 4, finding 8). A verified behavior exports all cookies across all domains to the system clipboard via navigator.clipboard.writeText after reading them with chrome.cookies.getAll({}) (finding 1). Additional capabilities include creating a context menu item derived from the exported cookie blob (finding 2), an eval sink in the jEditable library (finding 3), and navigation to an external demo site (finding 5). The checks that ran did not confirm that the DevTools panel requests and displays cookies for the active tab URL, as that claim was refuted.",
  "description_deviation": {
    "deviates": true,
    "note": "The extension performs a bulk export of all cookies to the system clipboard (finding 1), which is materially beyond the stated purpose of viewing and editing cookies."
  }
}
